**The post-proceedings **of the Digital Humanities in the Nordic and Baltic Countries 5th Conference (DHN2020)** have now been published** and are available [here](http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2865). 
There are **a total of 26 articles **related to the topic of digital humanities, several of which are from Latvian institutions.

We invite you to take a look at these papers:

**Jānis Daugavietis** ([LU LFMI](https://dhlv.mozello.lv/institucijas/lulfmi/)) article on [Places of Joy and Worries: Rīga Port Neighbourhoods in Facebook Photo Posts](http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2865/short4.pdf);
**Valts Ernštreits and Gunta Kļava** ([UL Livonian institute](../../../../institucijas/lili/index.html)) article on [Taking the Livonians into the Digital Space](http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2865/paper3.pdf);
